; KERNEL32.DEF
;
; The functions the Windows 98 SE / Me build may import from KERNEL32.dll:
; the import library is made from this list (llvm-dlltool -k), and
; tools/win9x_check.py fails a linked image that imports anything else.
;
; Each name here is exported and implemented by the KERNEL32 of Windows 98
; Second Edition and of Windows Me (Geoff Chappell's KERNEL32 export tables:
; first exported by 3.51/4.0 and not NT-only, or added in 4.10). None of
; the NT 4.0 additions 9x exports only as stubs (TryEnterCriticalSection,
; SwitchToThread, SignalObjectAndWait, the fibers), and of the W functions
; only the ones 9x implements (MultiByteToWideChar, WideCharToMultiByte,
; lstrlenW). In this copy (the DOS repository's Windows 95 build) none of
; 98's or 95 OSR2's additions either: GetFileAttributesExA and
; GetDiskFreeSpaceExA are left out (the C runtime looks the first up at run
; time), or the program would not start on the first Windows 95.

LIBRARY KERNEL32.dll
EXPORTS
CloseHandle@4
CompareFileTime@8
CopyFileA@12
CreateDirectoryA@8
CreateEventA@16
CreateFileA@28
CreateFileMappingA@24
CreateMutexA@12
CreateProcessA@40
CreateSemaphoreA@16
CreateThread@24
DebugBreak@0
DeleteCriticalSection@4
DeleteFileA@4
DuplicateHandle@28
EnterCriticalSection@4
ExitProcess@4
ExitThread@4
FileTimeToLocalFileTime@8
FileTimeToSystemTime@8
FindClose@4
FindFirstFileA@8
FindNextFileA@8
FlushFileBuffers@4
FlushInstructionCache@12
FormatMessageA@28
FreeLibrary@4
GetACP@0
GetCommandLineA@0
GetComputerNameA@8
GetCPInfo@8
GetCurrentDirectoryA@8
GetCurrentProcess@0
GetCurrentProcessId@0
GetCurrentThread@0
GetCurrentThreadId@0
GetDiskFreeSpaceA@20
GetDriveTypeA@4
GetEnvironmentVariableA@12
GetExitCodeThread@8
GetFileAttributesA@4
GetFileInformationByHandle@8
GetFileSize@8
GetFileTime@16
GetFileType@4
GetFullPathNameA@16
GetLastError@0
GetLocalTime@4
GetLogicalDrives@0
GetModuleFileNameA@12
GetModuleHandleA@4
GetOEMCP@0
GetPriorityClass@4
GetProcAddress@8
GetStartupInfoA@4
GetStdHandle@4
GetSystemDirectoryA@8
GetThreadContext@8
GetSystemInfo@4
GetSystemTime@4
GetSystemTimeAsFileTime@4
GetTempFileNameA@16
GetTempPathA@8
GetThreadPriority@4
GetTickCount@0
GetTimeZoneInformation@4
GetVersion@0
GetVersionExA@4
GetVolumeInformationA@32
GetWindowsDirectoryA@8
GlobalAlloc@8
GlobalFree@4
GlobalLock@4
GlobalMemoryStatus@4
GlobalUnlock@4
InitializeCriticalSection@4
IsBadCodePtr@4
IsBadReadPtr@8
IsBadWritePtr@8
IsDebuggerPresent@0
LeaveCriticalSection@4
LoadLibraryA@4
LocalAlloc@8
LocalFree@4
lstrcmpiA@8
lstrcpyA@8
lstrcpynA@12
lstrlenA@4
lstrlenW@4
MapViewOfFile@20
MapViewOfFileEx@24
MoveFileA@8
MultiByteToWideChar@24
OpenEventA@12
OutputDebugStringA@4
PeekNamedPipe@24
PulseEvent@4
QueryPerformanceCounter@4
QueryPerformanceFrequency@4
RaiseException@16
ReadFile@20
ReleaseMutex@4
ReleaseSemaphore@12
RemoveDirectoryA@4
ResetEvent@4
ResumeThread@4
SetConsoleCtrlHandler@8
SetCurrentDirectoryA@4
SetEndOfFile@4
SetEnvironmentVariableA@8
SetErrorMode@4
SetEvent@4
SetFileAttributesA@8
SetFilePointer@16
SetFileTime@16
SetLastError@4
SetPriorityClass@8
SetStdHandle@8
SetThreadPriority@8
SetUnhandledExceptionFilter@4
Sleep@4
SleepEx@8
SuspendThread@4
SystemTimeToFileTime@8
TerminateProcess@8
TlsAlloc@0
TlsFree@4
TlsGetValue@4
TlsSetValue@8
UnhandledExceptionFilter@4
UnmapViewOfFile@4
VirtualAlloc@16
VirtualFree@12
VirtualProtect@16
